// Title: Remote Access Tool - ScreenConnect Remote Command Execution - Hunting
// Sigma ID: d1a401ab-8c47-4e86-a7d8-2460b6a53e4a
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2024-02-23 | Modified: 2024-02-26
// ATT&CK: execution
// Tags: detection.threat-hunting
// Description: Detects remote binary or command execution via the ScreenConnect Service. Use this rule in order
//   to hunt for potentially anomalous executions originating from ScreenConnect
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate commands launched from ScreenConnect will also trigger this rule. Look for anomalies.
// References:
//   - https://www.huntress.com/blog/slashandgrab-screen-connect-post-exploitation-in-the-wild-cve-2024-1709-cve-2024-1708
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules-threat-hunting/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_remote_access_tools_screenconnect_child_proc.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\ScreenConnect.ClientService.exe"
